From: Nerves ROCK Pi S maintainers <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: rk3308: fix ramoops devicetree bugs

Two independent bugs left ramoops non-functional, so a kernel panic or
hard reset left nothing behind in /sys/fs/pstore to read back after
reboot:

1. ramoops_mem was a sibling of /reserved-memory instead of a child of
   it, so early_init_dt_scan_reserved_mem() never registered it. Worse,
   this kernel's ramoops driver (fs/pstore/ram.c, no
   RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE for "ramoops") doesn't actually resolve the
   region via the memory-region phandle at all - of_reserved_mem_lookup()
   matches the ramoops platform device's own node name ("ramoops")
   against the basename of a /reserved-memory child. The old
   "ramoops@110000" unit-address suffix never matched, so it always hit
   "ramoops: failed to locate DT /reserved-memory resource". Moving the
   node under /reserved-memory and dropping the unit address (naming it
   plainly "ramoops") makes the lookup-by-name succeed; the label is kept
   so the existing `memory-region = <&ramoops_mem>` reference still
   resolves for any future kernel that does honor it. `no-map` is added
   so the kernel never repurposes this RAM for anything else, which is
   required for the crash log to survive a panic uncorrupted.

2. record-size and console-size were written as 2-cell (64-bit) values
   (e.g. `<0x0 0x30000>`), but ramoops_parse_dt_u32() reads them with
   of_property_read_u32(), which only consumes the first cell - so both
   silently evaluated to 0. With no non-zero record/console size, probe
   failed with "The memory size and the record/console size must be
   non-zero" even after fix #1. Rewritten as single-cell values so the
   real sizes (0x30000 record + 0xc0000 console = the full 0xf0000
   region) are actually read.

Verified on hardware: after this patch, `dmesg | grep ramoops` shows
"using 0xf0000@0x110000" and "Registered ramoops as persistent store
backend" instead of the probe failure, and after a forced panic
(`echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger`) followed by reboot,
/sys/fs/pstore/dmesg-ramoops-0 contains the panic log.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308.dtsi | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3308.dtsi
@@ -355,17 +355,12 @@
 		method = "smc";
 	};

-	ramoops_mem: ramoops_mem {
-		reg = <0x0 0x110000 0x0 0xf0000>;
-		reg-names = "ramoops_mem";
-	};
-
 	ramoops: ramoops {
 		compatible = "ramoops";
-		record-size = <0x0 0x30000>;
-		console-size = <0x0 0xc0000>;
-		ftrace-size = <0x0 0x00000>;
-		pmsg-size = <0x0 0x00000>;
+		record-size = <0x30000>;
+		console-size = <0xc0000>;
+		ftrace-size = <0x0>;
+		pmsg-size = <0x0>;
 		memory-region = <&ramoops_mem>;
 	};

@@ -399,6 +394,11 @@
 		#size-cells = <2>;
 		ranges;

+		ramoops_mem: ramoops {
+			reg = <0x0 0x110000 0x0 0xf0000>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
 		drm_logo: drm-logo@00000000 {
 			compatible = "rockchip,drm-logo";
 			reg = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
